# ---- BOOK-1 interaction props (generated by tools/book/compile.py; scripts.json refers to them by id) ----
# iprop <floor> <room> <id> <kind> <x> <z> <yaw> "<label>"    an interactable prop (instanced per kind); yaw 0 faces +z / south
# islot <floor> <room> <id> <kind> <x> <z> <yaw>             a named interaction point (NPC stand / seat) used by scripts
# a trailing on_model = the institute model already has this piece of furniture there (its podium, shelf, poster, chair): no new mesh
# prop kinds (prop_kinds.json; w x d metres across x along the facing direction; wall = flush against a wall):
#   poster       0.70 x 0.05  wall  existing  framed wall poster (corridor posters of MAP-2)
#   plaque       0.40 x 0.04  wall  existing  small wall plaque, like the coloured door signs
#   board        1.60 x 0.10  wall  existing  whiteboard (MAP-2 PROP board)
#   lightbox     0.90 x 0.10  wall  existing  X-ray / figure viewer on the wall (MAP-2 PROP lightbox)
#   shelf        1.20 x 0.40  wall  existing  shelf unit against a wall: books, drugs, specimens (MAP-2 shelf)
#   cabinet      0.80 x 0.50  wall  existing  filing / storage cabinet (MAP-2 cabinet)
#   counter      1.60 x 0.60  wall  existing  dispensing counter (map slot kind counter)
#   bench        1.80 x 0.70  wall  existing  lab bench (map slot kind bench)
#   cart         0.70 x 0.50  free  existing  trolley; used as the bedside chart trolley (MAP-2 PROP cart)
#   monitor      0.50 x 0.50  free  existing  monitor on a stand; also OR screen and breath analyser (MAP-2 monitor)
#   scope_tower  0.70 x 0.60  free  existing  endoscopy tower (MAP-2 trolleyTower)
#   model        0.50 x 0.50  free  existing  anatomical model on a stand (MAP-2 PROP model)
#   podium       0.60 x 0.50  free  existing  lectern (MAP-2 PROP podium)
#   microscope   0.80 x 0.60  free  new       small lab table with a microscope; footprint 0.8 x 0.6 m, height 1.2 m
#   iv_stand     0.50 x 0.50  free  new       IV pole on a 5-wheel base with a drip bag; footprint 0.5 x 0.5 m, height 1.9 m
